:: Fishing Combat Beach
<<effects>>
<<run fishingCombatEffects()>>

/* Player orgasm */
<<if $arousal gte $arousalmax>>
	<<if $daily.fishing.beach.fisher.phase is "fishing">>
		<<fishCombatBeachOrgasmFisher>>
	<<else>>
		<<fishCombatBeachOrgasm>>
	<</if>>

/* You've caught the fish */
<<elseif $fishing.combat.fishDistance lte 0>>
	<<if Weather.dayState is "day" and ($daily.fishing.beach.fisher.phase is "finished" or $daily.fishing.beach.fisher.phase is undefined) and random(1, 12) is 1 and $daily.fishing.seagullSteal is undefined>>
		<<fishingSeagullCaught "beach">>
	<<elseif $daily.fishing.beach.fisher.phase is "fishing" and $daily.fishing.beach.fisher.drunk gte 1 and random(1, 5) is 1>>
		<<fishCombatBeachCaughtFisherDrunk>>
	<<elseif beachCampfirePartyPresent() and random(1, 4) is 1 and $daily.fishing.beach.partyFeed is undefined and canCookFish($fishingHookedFish.type, $fishingHookedFish.size)>>
		<<fishCombatBeachCaughtCampfireCook>>
	<<else>>
		<<fishCombatBeachCaught>>
	<</if>>

/* Your line has snapped */
<<elseif $fishing.combat.lineHealth lte 0>>
	<<fishCombatBeachLineSnapped>>

/* Still fishing */
<<else>>
	<<fishCombatBeachMain>>

<</if>>


:: Fishing Beach Cut Line
<<effects>>
<<run endFishingCombat()>>
You release the tension on the rod, letting the line go slack. The <<print $fishingHookedFish.type>> pulls harder, and with a sudden snap, the line breaks free. Through the ripples, you catch a glimpse of it darting deeper, finally free.
<<unset $fishingHookedFish>>
<br><br>

<<link [[Re-hook the line and cast back out (0:03)|Fishing Beach Wait]]>><<pass 3>><</link>>
<br>
<<link [[Leave|Beach]]>><<set $eventskip to 1>><</link>>


:: Widgets Fishing Combat Beach [widget]
<<widget "fishCombatBeachMain">>
	<<run fishCombatAction()>>
	<<fishCombatActionDescription>>
	<<printFishInfo>>
	<br><br>

	<<fishCombatActions "Beach">>
	<<fishingBeachCombatDebugLinks>>
<</widget>>

<<widget "fishCombatBeachCaught">>
	<<set _canEatFish to canEatFishTf($fishingHookedFish)>>
	<<run updateFishRecord($fishingHookedFish.type, $fishingHookedFish.size, "beach")>>
	<<run endFishingCombat()>>
	<<run holdCaughtFish($fishingHookedFish.type)>>

	<<fishingCatchFishText "beach">>
	<br><br>

	<<if _canEatFish>>
		It's such a small fish, you could probably fit the whole thing in your mouth.
		<br><br>
	<</if>>

	<<if _canEatFish>>
		<<link [[Eat the fish|Fishing Beach Cat Eat]]>><</link>>
		<br><br>
	<</if>>

	<<link [[Stow it away|Fishing Beach Keep]]>><</link>>
	<br>
	<<link [["Throw the " + $fishingHookedFish.type + " back"|Fishing Beach Throw Back]]>><</link>>
<</widget>>

<<widget "fishCombatBeachLineSnapped">>
	Your line suddenly goes slack, and the <<print $fishingHookedFish.type>> disappears into the depths.
	<<run endFishingCombat()>>
	<<unset $fishingHookedFish>>
	<br><br>

	<<link [[Re-hook the line and cast back out (0:03)|Fishing Beach Wait]]>><<pass 3>><</link>>
	<br>
	<<link [[Leave|Beach]]>><<set $eventskip to 1>><</link>>
<</widget>>

<<widget "fishCombatBeachOrgasm">>
	<<orgasmFishingBeach>>
	The rod slips from your grip. By the time you recover, the line has gone slack, the <<print $fishingHookedFish.type>> is long gone.
	<<run endFishingCombat()>>
	<<unset $fishingHookedFish>>
	<br>
	<<link [[Next|Fishing Beach Wait]]>><</link>>
<</widget>>
